      "role": "assistant",
      "reasoning": "Confirm closed triangle and connect to option A. Provide mandatory formula breakdown and exam tip.",
      "content": "A closed triangle indicates a zero resultant vector. Therefore, the correct option is A.\n\n**Final Answer:** A\n\n---\n### 📖 Formula Breakdown (How It Works):\n* **The Formula:** $\\sum \\vec{F} = 0$\n* **What the letters mean:**\n  * $\\sum \\vec{F}$ is the vector sum of all forces acting on the object (measured in Newtons, $\\text{N}$)\n  * $0$ represents translational equilibrium (no net force, meaning constant velocity or stationary)\n* **Why we use it:** According to Newton's First Law, when forces are in equilibrium, placing them tip-to-tail creates a closed polygon (or a triangle for three forces) because the vector sum returns to the starting point.\n\n🎯 **Exam Tip:** Always check the direction of the arrowheads! For a closed vector diagram representing equilibrium, the arrows must follow each other continuously around the loop (head-to-tail), rather than colliding head-on."
