      "content": "Take a deep breath. 🌸 You are going to be okay, and we will figure this out together step-by-step. Physics can feel overwhelming when you're stressed, but wave diffraction is just about how waves bend around obstacles.\n\nThink about standing outside a room with an open door. If someone plays a deep bass note (long wavelengths), you hear it clearly all around the room because the sound waves bend (diffract) easily around the door frame. If someone plays a high-pitched whistle (short wavelengths), it travels in a straight beam and doesn't bend as much.\n\nRelating this to light: red light and blue light have very different wavelengths. Before we look at the options, do you remember which colour has the longer wavelength — red or blue?"
